    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 302136\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n236 PM PDT Wed Sep 30 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Mild weather and warming temperatures are expected through the \n  weekend into early next week. \n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...through Tuesday.\n\nA broad ridge of high pressure is building in over the Desert  \nSouthwest in the wake of the tropical moisture-infused trough that \nbrought us all the active weather over the past few day. We will \nsee a big bump in temperatures today under clear skies, returning \nthe forecast area to above normal temperatures. After today, there\nwill be a slow warming trend, peaking over the weekend with high \ntemperatures near 10 degrees above normal by Sunday.\n\nEarly next week, a shortwave associated with a dampening trough \nof low pressure in the eastern Pacific may influence temperatures\nMonday and Tuesday, but there has been a weakening trend in\nguidance so confidence is low in this feature's development at \nthis time.\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 00Z Forecast Package...Light\nwinds will follow typical daily directional patterns with some \nvariability through the forecast period, with speeds under 8KT. \nVFR conditions and clear skies prevail.\n\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast\nCalifornia...For the 00Z Forecast Package...Winds will remain\naround 5-10KT across the region the next 24 hours, following \ntypical daily directional patterns with some variability. VFR \nconditions with clear skies continue. \n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Berc\nAVIATION...Phillipson\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
